; The demos and the art they are built from: one small world per engine
; feature, plus the five-room showcase level that has all of them at once.
; Nothing in the engine depends on any of this, which is the point: it is
; content, and it lives outside the library it is content for.
;
; camlcast is the only dependency, SDL included: a demo that binds a key names
; a Camlcast.Key and never reaches past the engine for it, the same way a game
; does.

; The public name is the package name, so this installs as lib/camlcast-demo/
; and camlcast.install carries none of it. It was camlcast.demo, whose first
; component names the package a public name belongs to — which put a findlib
; subpackage, and every .ml in this directory, into the engine's own install
; file: the content shipped with the library it is content for, and the demos
; missing from the package that is the demos.
;
; The executable in bin/ has this same public name and does not collide with it:
; one is a binary in bin/, the other a findlib package in lib/. The module name
; is untouched — it comes from (name) — so every `open Camlcast_demo` and every
; (libraries camlcast_demo) still reads the same.

(library
 (name camlcast_demo)
 (public_name camlcast-demo)
 (libraries camlcast))
